      "side": 1,
      "message": "In fact, I was using readParcelableList in the patchset1 but I found there is a problem that readParcelableList cannot support the case if underlyingNetworks is null.\nIn readParcelableList, it asks the caller to pass a non-null list and if readInt() returns -1, readParcelableList just clear the list that we passed into.\nIn this case, we don\u0027t know the underlyingNetwork is null or an empty list before.\nSo I check readInt() by ourselves and set underlyingNetworks to null if readInt() returns -1.\n\nAdded a comment to describe why we don\u0027t use readParcelableList, see if it works for you.\n\n```\npublic final \u003cT extends Parcelable\u003e List\u003cT\u003e readParcelableList(\n        @NonNull List\u003cT\u003e list, @Nullable ClassLoader cl) {\n    final int N \u003d readInt();\n    if (N \u003d\u003d -1) {\n        list.clear();\n        return list;\n    }\n    ...\n    ...\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "e2fe0a84_a0cd8b85",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2041,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2048,
        "endChar": 17
      },
